.TH PSSoftmax 3 2025-01-20 "PsyC 0.9.5" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSSoftmax\fR \- Softmax function

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/activation.h>

.I
void  
.br
\fBPSSoftmax\fR(\fIPSFloat *vec\fR, \fIPSFloat *dest\fR, \fIlong len\fR, \fIint acceleration\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Computes Softmax function on vector \fIvec\fR of length \fIlen\fR. Result is stored into vector \fIdest\fR. If \fIdest\fR is \fINULL\fR, result will be stored into \fIvec\fR itself.
.br
For the \fIacceleration\fR argument, take a look at \fIPSAcceleration\fR.
.br
The Softmax function can be used to get the probability distribution from a series of numbers.
.br
For more info about Softmax:
.br
    \fIhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Softmax_function\fR

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1)
